== Additional facts ==
- Driver opt level is output-neutral: -O0-driver eager body == -O2-driver eager body (cmp clean).
- Rust-emitted lower_expr_inner ALSO has dead decls: 6,308 of 15,691 (~40%) — Fix A mirrors to src/backend/c_lir.
- The deep expr: derive.gg:172 (gen Serializable Dict-field writer), single return with 51 ` + ` ops;
  crash bt outer frames (lower_closures___lower_function -> lower_stmt -> lower_if) match its if/return shape.
- Stock-Linux 8MB ulimit would kill even the RUST-BUILT stage-0 on this recursion
  (51 x 192.4KB = 9.81MB): the whole bootstrap apparatus currently depends on raised stack limits
  (this box: ulimit -s 12500).
- fixed_point cargo test deadlines: stage emissions have a hardcoded 600s deadline each;
  -O0 eager stage-0 emission here = 377s (fits); flip adds ~11%.
- Guard census: lower_expr_inner 30->78 clone_to_owned sites (+48; family root `ctx`,
  members dict_kname/dict_vname/joins), lower_call 14 lazy. Module-wide 927->1071 (+144).
- Main-emission sites for Fix B (big-stack runner): src/backend/c_lir/mod.rs:1064,
  self-host lir_codegen.gg emit_function main arm (~:4755).

== Executable guard recommendation (CLAUDE.md invariant 6) ==
Add a deep-recursion canary fixture (e.g. a ~200-term `a + b + ...` concat chain, or
programmatic nesting) compiled THROUGH the self-host driver in the gated battery:
without a structural fix it overflows on ANY box; with Fix B (big-stack main) it passes
everywhere. Converts the silent environment-coupled cliff (bootstrap green only because
ulimit -s >= ~12MB) into a loud test.

== -O0 driver timing pair (idle box, sequential, same -O0 stage-0 binary) ==
O0-EAGER 377s | O0-LAZY 368s  => 0.98x (lazy ~= eager; within noise).
Combined with the -O2 pair (295s/327s = 1.11x): the "~7x lazy-emission slowdown"
DOES NOT REPRODUCE under controlled conditions at either opt level. Most plausible
origin of the prior 363s-vs-50s figure: lazy run measured under parallel cargo-test
CPU thrash (the documented 4-8x wall multiplier) vs an idle eager baseline.
